Description: Converts a single-cell dataset with donor labels into an effective
    sample size, a minimum detectable effect, and a prescription of how many
    additional donors are required to support a target effect. Donor-level
    biological variance is separated from the residual technical variance of the
    pseudobulk mean by resampling each donor's own cells at the depth that donor
    has, so the depth penalty is measured rather than assumed. The minimum
    detectable effect uses exact t quantiles at the design degrees of freedom
    instead of the normal approximation, and the prescription is solved by
    bisection.
